(II)--a son of दशरथ known for his righteous- ness and truth: परिक्षित् compared to him: An अवतार् of Hari born in the इक्ष्वाकु line; killed रावण; His fame equalled that of पृथु.
1: भा. I. १२. १९; II. 7. २३-25; IV. २२. ६३; IX. १०. 3; M. १२. ५०-51.
King of the कोशल country and brother of लक्ष्मण, Bharata, and शत्रुघ्न: Disfigured सूर्पणका; killed मारीच (सुबाहु?) and other राक्षसस् in the यज्ञ of विश्वामित्र, bent and broke the bow of शिव and married सीता, put down the pride of परशुराम, spent a forest life with his wife in obedience to his father's command, killed Khara, त्रिशिरस् and १४,000 राक्षसस्; performed the funeral rites to जटायु, and Kabandha, killed वालि for the sake of सुग्रीव, put up a bridge across the sea, welcomed by the Lord of the seas; killed रावण and कुम्भकर्ण in their capital, ordered विभीषण to perform funeral rites to his dead kith and kin; recovered सीता; enthroned विभी- षण; left in an aerial chariot to अयोध्या, embraced Bharata, paid respects to Brahmanas, Gurus, elders and was crowned by वसिष्ठ just like Indra. In his period which was the त्रेतायुग, it looked like कृतयुग; sons, कुश and Lava; ruled for १०१० years;
2: भा. V. १९. 1; VII. 1. ४४; १०. ३६; IX. १०. 3-५२; X. ४०. २०; XI. 4. २१; Br. III. 7. २०३; 8. ५४; ३७. ३०; ६३. १८५-193; ६४. १६; ७३. ९१; वा. ८८. १९२-4; Vi. IV. 4. ८७-102, १०४.
led an exemplary household life, by his loyalty to his wedded wife; performed sacrifices by giv- ing all his kingdom as दक्षिण, retaining only the ornaments and dress, and for सीता, her सौमान्गल्य। The Brahmanas returned the kingdom as they had no use for it and praised him.
3: भा. IX. १०. ५३-6; ११. 1-7; वा. ७०. ४८; ८८, १८४, १९१-7.
One night he went about to know what people talked of his rule. He heard a person saying that राम was mad after सीता, taking her back though she was at another's house for long. Next day he abandoned her and left her at वाल्- मीकि's abode. Here were born his two sons--कुश and Lava. When सीता entered the bowels of the earth, राम led a life of celibacy for १३,000 years giving joy and happiness to the people of कोशल. Sent his brothers on दिग्विजय and him- self resided at the capital.
4: भा. IX. ११. 8-३५.
Hearing of the रामचरित of वाल्- मीकि, rids one of कर्मबन्धस्;
5: Ib. IX. ११. २३; M. १२. ५०-51.
resided on the banks of the कदली river;
6: Ib. २२. ५३.
